Error [jet.InteriorNulByte]: This string literal has an embedded NUL byte, so it can't cross into a C function.
  --> tests/ui/cffi_string_literal_interior_nul.jet:10:18
    |
 12 |     print(c.grab("a\u{0000}b"))
    |                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: C strings are NUL-terminated, not length-prefixed — an embedded `\0` would truncate the string on the C side, silently losing everything after it.
 Fix: Remove the embedded NUL, or split the call so the C function only sees the part before it.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3211
